:: the_guild__guild_hall [the_guild]
<!-- harness:meta
location: guild_hall
-->

The Cartographers' Guild sits behind a facade of unmarked stone on Brassmaker's Row. You have been inside a hundred times for audits and license renewals. It has never felt like this.

The Hallmaster, Aldric Voss, is waiting for you in the inner chamber. He is an old man made of maps; there is ink in his veins, they say, and his skin has the yellow sheen of old parchment. He does not look angry. He looks afraid.

"Sit," he says. The chair is hard wood. "You know why you are here."

He slides a map across the table. It is your Veilwood map. The one you burned. It is whole. The blue ink still glistens.

"We found this in your stove," Voss says. "Fire does not touch maps that have been *written true*. You have crossed a line, cartographer. You are not describing the world anymore."

<<set $guild_trust to $guild_trust - 1>>

